<BlogPost title="Nevara Cabinetry by WW Wood: Premium Plywood at Value Pricing" description="Nevara frameless cabinetry sits 50% below Eclipse while offering full 3/4-inch plywood construction and soft-close performance." author="Ben Miller" publishedDate="2025-07-22" modifiedDate="2026-10-29">

<blockquote><strong>Update (March 2026):</strong> Nevara formally launched on March 27, 2026 with its own multiplier (your Shiloh multiplier × 0.95), the v2.0 price book, and an estimated 3–4 week lead time. The pricing and lead-time notes below are from the pre-launch period — see <a href="/playbook/nevara-cabinets-launch-2026/">Nevara Cabinets Officially Launches</a> for current quoting rules.</blockquote>

<p>Looking for a frameless cabinet line that offers premium plywood construction without premium pricing? Meet Nevara, the latest offering from WW Wood Products — your go-to choice for budget-conscious clients who still expect quality.</p>

<blockquote>"Nevara is built like a tank — but priced like a compact."</blockquote>

<p>This line was designed to sit about 50% below the cost of <a href="/brands/eclipse-cabinetry/">Eclipse</a>, while still boasting full 3/4" plywood construction and soft-close performance.</p>

<h2>Why Dealers Are Taking Notice</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Frameless Cabinetry:</strong> Fully assembled by WW Wood in Missouri, 3/4" plywood box</li>
<li><strong>White Shaker Standard:</strong> Ships in a painted white 5-piece MDF door (Westbridge style)</li>
<li><strong>Fast Turnaround:</strong> estimated 3–4 week lead time, with a dedicated Nevara multiplier (<a href="/playbook/nevara-cabinets-launch-2026/">details</a>)</li>
<li><strong>Spec Support:</strong> Spec books, catalogs, and order forms ready to go</li>
</ul>

<h2>Build Highlights</h2>
<ul>
<li>Blum soft-close concealed hinges (adjustable)</li>
<li>5/8" dovetailed solid wood drawers</li>
<li>3/4" thick adjustable plywood shelves</li>
<li>Fully edge-banded panels</li>
</ul>

<h2>Who's This Right For?</h2>
<p>Homes upgrading from in-stock cabinets, builders hitting a price point but wanting WW Wood reliability, and clients who want real wood construction without color customization. A win for quality, price, and simplicity.</p>

